        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-7> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion Partial Differential Equations (PDE)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 3.8e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Section headers and docstrings describe the Gray-Scott PDE and FFT ring metrics (L160-313), but functions lack explicit equation, section, and figure mappings to Turing (1952) Sections 8-9, Pearson (1993) Eq. 1 & Fig. 1-2, and Kondo & Asai (1995) Fig. 1-3." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-code-traceability> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1952-turing-morpho.py L162–L221: solver functions lack explicit paper section/equation citations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L162-L221>" ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 54/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/turing-gray-scott-1> ;
    rdfs:comment "Integrates the 2D periodic Gray-Scott PDE dU/dt = Du*Lap(U) - U*V^2 + F*(1-U), dV/dt = Dv*Lap(V) + U*V^2 - (F+k)*V (L162-221) with Du/Dv = 2.0. However, as identified by the independent second assessor (Claude Sonnet 5.5 High): (1) Turing (1952) is not implemented at all—there is no linearized 2-morphogen reaction-diffusion system, no dispersion relation sigma(k^2), no critical wavenumber k_c, and no ring-of-20-cells model; (2) Pearson's (1993) saddle-node bifurcation curve 4*(F+k)^2 = F and Hopf boundary are not computed, and 3 of the 4 patterned regimes lie past the saddle-node boundary where no nontrivial homogeneous steady state exists; and (3) the equal-diffusion control (Du=Dv=0.10, L147-155) halves Du and tests finite-amplitude front extinction toward the always-stable trivial state (1,0) rather than linear Turing instability around a homogeneous steady state." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1952-turing-morpho.py L100–L156: PEARSON_REGIMES with 4 patterned points + flawed Du=Dv=0.10 trivial-state extinction control <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L100-L156>",
        "1952-turing-morpho.py L162–L221: 5-point periodic Gray-Scott forward Euler solver without Turing (1952) linear dispersion or Pearson bifurcation boundaries <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L162-L221>" ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 30/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes 2D Hann-windowed FFT radial PSD, azimuthal m=2/m=6 harmonics, and connected-component Euler characteristic (L227-313), but all metrics are purely self-referential without comparison to analytical Turing wavelength lambda_c = 2*pi/k_c, Pearson's (1993) phase boundaries, or Kondo & Asai (1995) empirical stripe wavelengths. Moreover, integer-binned k* gives k* = 11, 12, 12, 11 cycles across all four patterned regimes, failing to resolve sub-bin wavelength shifts. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): dominant wavelength (last frame) = 50.0 grid cells [peak of the radial power spectrum of the axes-box image, scaled to the N=200 grid] — Gray–Scott f=0.055,k=0.062 labyrinth; no specimen or literature wavelength recorded; pattern coverage (last frame) = 0.0059 fraction [fraction of axes box in the high-V (yellow) band]; connected high-V components (last frame) = 101 count [scipy.ndimage.label on the yellow mask]; fraction of pattern pixels changed, first→last frame = 0.0 fraction (reference >0 for an evolving simulation) [XOR of yellow masks of frame 0 and the last frame] — ≈0 means the GIF shows a frozen pattern; Pearson coral labyrinth (F=0.055, k=0.062) spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.0 cycles / domain (reference >0 (Turing band-pass ring), Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern η/γ) [peak of 2D radial PSD P(k) on N=160x160 grid after 4000 steps] — λ* = 14.55 grid cells, ring sharpness = 718.1; Pearson mitosis spots (F=0.028, k=0.062) connected components vs coral labyrinth = 129 count (reference 14, Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern λ/θ vs Pattern η/γ) [connected high-activator components in self-replicating spot regime] — spots remain disconnected (>100 components) whereas coral labyrinth percolates; equal-diffusion negative control (Du=Dv=0.10) spectral wavenumber k* = 0.0 cycles / domain (reference 0.0, Turing 1952 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37 (diffusion-driven instability requires Du != Dv)) [dominant wavenumber when differential diffusivity is removed (Du = Dv = 0.10 at F=0.055, k=0.062)] — spatial σ_V = 0.00e+00, ring sharpness = 0.0." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1952-turing-morpho.py L270–L286: integer-binned k_star_idx = argmax(radial_psd) yields identical 11-12 bin values across regimes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L270-L286>",
        "turing_pearson_metrics.csv L1–L6: self-referential FFT metrics with no analytical lambda_c or biological benchmark comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/turing_pearson_metrics.csv#L1-L6>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-7> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 38.0/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Pass 1 (v1) dual-agent evaluation of `1952-turing-morpho.py` (Gemini 4 Argon + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High consensus: 39.6/100). The v1 script integrates the 2D Gray-Scott PDE across 4 hardcoded (F, k) regimes plus an equal-diffusion control and computes 2D FFT radial power spectra, but completely omits Turing's (1952) linear reaction-diffusion instability equations, dispersion relation sigma(k^2), and ring-of-20-cells model; omits Pearson's (1993) saddle-node (4(F+k)^2 = F) and Hopf bifurcation curves; uses a conceptually flawed trivial-state extinction control for Du=Dv; has zero biological specimen images or segmentation (no Kondo & Asai 1995 Pomacanthus stripe spacing or Y-junction analysis); and lacks a vendored `datasets/turing/` reference package with SHA-256 verification. Overall 38.0/100 (faithfulness 32.3, reproducibility 51.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 54, Morphological realism / specimen match 14, Parameter expressivity 38, Morphometric validation 30, Source and data traceability 45, Code-to-model traceability 45, Reproducibility package 61. Output judged: turing_pearson_morphospace.png: rendered output of 1952-turing-morpho.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1206789 B, 2421×1240 px, artifact_sha256 545bf3f8f507c4ca509d4fd02333e3c3a2977b267973a82eb904816743575163 (sha256 545bf3f8f507c4ca509d4fd02333e3c3a2977b267973a82eb904816743575163), spec_fingerprint 457ba1d8776c5109e7d828595ec1ea637e0d9b8eebcf725fc073d1f70566f695. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 457ba1d8776c5109e7d828595ec1ea637e0d9b8eebcf725fc073d1f70566f695; artifact_sha256: 545bf3f8f507c4ca509d4fd02333e3c3a2977b267973a82eb904816743575163." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement Pearson (1993) exact Saddle-Node (4*(F+k)^2 = F) and Hopf bifurcation curves, map all 12 Pearson pattern classes (alpha through mu) on the (F, k) phase diagram, and replace the flawed trivial-state extinction control with a true diffusivity-ratio sweep (d = Du/Dv across the analytical Turing threshold d_c around a nontrivial steady state).",
        "remediation needed: Implement Turing (1952) Section 8-9 two-morphogen linear reaction-diffusion dispersion relation sigma(k^2), critical wavenumber k_c, analytical wavelength lambda_c = 2*pi/k_c, and Turing's N=20 ring-of-cells morphogenesis model.",
        "remediation needed: Upgrade spectral morphometrics to sub-bin parabolic/centroid wavenumber estimation, compare measured wavelengths against analytical lambda_c and empirical Pomacanthus stripe spacing, expose full CLI parameters, sync `docs/media/turing_gray_scott.gif`, and formalize Turing dispersion & Pearson saddle-node theorems in `morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean` Section 5.",
        "remediation needed: Vendor `datasets/turing/` with SHA-256-locked reference data (Turing 1952 ring parameters, Pearson 1993 12-regime table, Kondo & Asai 1995 Pomacanthus stripe spacing table) plus real CC-licensed biological specimen photographs (Pomacanthus semicirculatus skin stripes & Tetraodon/Ostracion hexagonal spots), and segment the biological stripes, inter-stripe wavelength, and Y-branch dislocations directly in `1952-turing-morpho.py`." ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 38/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Only 4 patterned (F, k) points plus 1 control are hardcoded in `PEARSON_REGIMES` (L100-156), omitting Pearson's (1993) 12 pattern classes (alpha through mu) and (F, k) phase diagram. No CLI arguments exist for F, k, Du, Dv, N, steps, dt, or seed (L561-580), and no continuous parameter sweep of diffusivity ratio d = Du/Dv or feed/kill rates is performed." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1952-turing-morpho.py L100–L156: hardcoded 5-element tuple without Pearson's 12 pattern classes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L100-L156>",
        "1952-turing-morpho.py L561–L580: CLI exposes only --no-show, --skip-gif, --self-test, --output-png, --output-csv <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L561-L580>" ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-turing-gray-scott-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Reproducibility package: 61/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Uses deterministic `np.random.default_rng(1952)` and includes `--self-test`, `--no-show`, and `--skip-gif` flags (L511-591). However, `--self-test` uses overly loose thresholds (`ring_sharpness > 5.0` when observed values are 718-967), does not verify two-run hash determinism, and `render_legacy_neon_gif` writes `turing_patterns_black_neon.gif` (N=200, 5000 steps) out of sync with `docs/media/turing_gray_scott.gif`." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-repro-package> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1952-turing-morpho.py L319–L364: render_legacy_neon_gif writes turing_patterns_black_neon.gif rather than updating docs/media/turing_gray_scott.gif <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L319-L364>",
        "1952-turing-morpho.py L528–L557: loose self_test thresholds (sharpness > 5.0) and no determinism check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1952-turing-morpho.py#L528-L557>" ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

